<title>UK: BASKETBALL-MEN'S EUROLEAGUE RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BASKETBALL-MEN'S EUROLEAGUE RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in men's EuroLeague</p>
<p>basketball matches on Thursday, final day of last round-robin</p>
<p>matches in opening phase. Second phase starts on January 9:</p>
<p>In Athens: Panionios (Greece) 79 Stefanel Milan (Italy) 86</p>
<p>(halftime 35- 38).</p>
<p>Top Scorers:</p>
<p>Panionios - Mitchell Wiggins 22, Fanis Christodoulou 18,</p>
<p>George Kalaitzis 15</p>
<p>Stefanel - Gregor Fucka 19, Ferdinando Gentile 15, Antony</p>
<p>Bowie 12</p>
<p>Attendance: 2,500</p>
<p>Group A</p>
<p>In Limoges: Limoges (France) 83 CSKA Moscow (Russia) 66</p>
<p>(37-24)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Limoges - Yann Bonato 20, Frederic Forte 16, Gerald Glass 13</p>
<p>Moscow - Sergei Bazarevitch 15, Valery Daineko 13, Sergei</p>
<p>Panov 12.</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,000</p>
<p>In Tel Aviv: Maccabi Tel Aviv (Israel) 71, Ulker Spor</p>
<p>(Turkey) 65 (32-36)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Maccabi: Constantin Popa 18, Brad Leaf 14, Buck Johnson 14</p>
<p>Ulker: Orhun Ena 21, Dan Godfread 14</p>
<p>Group D:</p>
<p>In Belgrade: Partizan Belgrade (Yugoslavia) 97 Dynamo Moscow</p>
<p>(Russia) 64 (47-27)</p>
<p>In Bologna: Kinder Bologna (Italy) 86 Pau Orthez (France) 74 (43-38)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Bologna - Komazec 25, Savic 14, Patavoukas 13, Abbio 13</p>
<p>Pau - Foirest 16, Fauthoux 15, Bryn 12, Crowder 11</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,600</p>
<p>In Seville: Sevilla (Spain) 68 Efes Pilsen (Turkey) 70 (31-42)</p>
<p>Group B</p>
<p>In Madrid: Estudiantes (Spain) 87 Olympiakos (Greece) 78 (35-40)  </p>
<p>In Charleroi: Charleroi (Belgium) 69 Alba Berlin (Germany)</p>
<p>79 (45-35).</p>
